@startuml
title FIGURA 3. ARQUITECTURA DE INVENTARIO-SERVICE

top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Sistema de Pedidos\nCliente REST" as Client

package "CAPA API - JAX-RS" {
    [RestApplication\n/api] as Application
    [ProductoResource\n/inventario/productos] as Resource

    [ConstraintViolationExceptionMapper] as ValidationMapper
    [InventarioExceptionMapper] as ExceptionMapper
}

package "CAPA DE SERVICIOS" {
    [InventarioService\n@Stateless] as Service
    [InventarioException] as Exception
}

package "CAPA DE DOMINIO" {
    [ProductoInventario\n@Entity] as Product
}

package "CAPA DTO" {
    [ProductoResponse]
    [ReservaStockRequest]
    [ReservaStockResponse]
    [StockResponse]
    [ApiError]
}

database "MySQL\nInventarioDB" as DB

Client --> Application : HTTP
Application --> Resource : Enrutamiento REST

Resource --> Service : Operaciones de inventario
Resource --> Product : DTO / respuesta

Service --> Product : Gestión de entidades
Product --> DB : JPA / EntityManager

Resource --> ValidationMapper : Errores de validación
Resource --> ExceptionMapper : Excepciones

Service --> Exception : Errores de negocio

Resource --> ProductoResponse
Resource --> ReservaStockRequest
Resource --> ReservaStockResponse
Resource --> StockResponse

note right of Service
Operaciones principales:
- Listar productos
- Obtener por ID
- Obtener por código
- Reservar stock
- Consultar stock
end note

note bottom of DB
Persistencia:
producto_inventario

Incluye precio, stock,
código y versión.
end note

@enduml